examples.description:
int i = 0;
f(++i, ++i);
Before C++17, the behavior is undefined, so the behavior could be anything (e.g., 
f(2, 2)
).
Since C++17, this code does not have undefined behavior, but it is still not specified which argument is evaluated first. The call will be 
f(1, 2)
 or 
f(2, 1)
, but you don’t know which.

