content:
Reason

Performance is very sensitive to cache performance, and cache algorithms favor simple (usually linear) access to adjacent data.

Example

int matrix[rows][cols];

// bad
for (int c = 0; c < cols; ++c)
 for (int r = 0; r < rows; ++r)
 sum += matrix[r][c];

// good
for (int r = 0; r < rows; ++r)
 for (int c = 0; c < cols; ++c)
 sum += matrix[r][c];

