examples.description:
Assume you wanted to write
void func(zstring arg)
{
 Gadget g {arg};
 // ...
}
If the 
gadget
 isn’t correctly constructed, 
func
 exits with an exception.
If we cannot throw an exception, we can simulate this RAII style of resource handling by adding a 
valid()
 member function to 
Gadget
:
error_indicator func(zstring arg)
{
 Gadget g {arg};
 if (!g.valid()) return gadget_construction_error;
 // ...
 return 0; // zero indicates "good"
}
The problem is of course that the caller now has to remember to test the return value. To encourage doing so, consider adding a 
[[nodiscard]]
.
