Reason

Improved readability.
Implementation hiding.
Note that template aliases replace many uses of traits to compute a type.
They can also be used to wrap a trait.

Example

template<typename T, size_t N>
class Matrix {
 // ...
 using Iterator = typename std::vector<T>::iterator;
 // ...
};

This saves the user of 
Matrix
 from having to know that its elements are stored in a 
vector
 and also saves the user from repeatedly typing 
typename std::vector<T>::
.

Example

